# cssom-heads.baseline — the exact authored-rule-head count of app.css.
#
# cssom-parity.mjs asserts authoredHeads(app.css) == this number (EXACT, not >=).
# A /* swallow drops the count and reds; a new rule raises it and reds — until you
# bump this number IN THE SAME COMMIT as the CSS change. That co-commit is the whole
# ratchet: the count can only move through a reviewed diff, never drift. See
# cssom-parity.mjs "THE EXACT-MATCH SIDECAR RATCHET" for why not git-derived and why
# not a relative tolerance.
#
# Measured 2026-07-21 on app.css @ sha256 176f441387bc… (Chrome 150.0.7871.129,
# node v22.22.0): 1203 authored heads == 1203 CSSOM rules, MISSES 0.
#
# Re-measured 2026-07-28 by running cssom-parity.mjs on this branch merged with
# origin/main: 1235 authored heads, MISSES 0 — the +2 are the Overview's own
# not-current chip rules. MISSES 0 is what makes this an unrecorded ADD rather
# than a parity defect, which is the distinction the ratchet's own failure text
# tells you to confirm before bumping.
#
# Re-measured 2026-07-31 (W12 narrow-viewport slice, cch-w12-s2): UNCHANGED at
# 1235, MISSES 0 — deliberately NOT bumped. That slice edits app.css in two
# regions but adds no rule HEAD: `.instances-grid`, `.set-matrix`,
# `.set-matrix-corner` and `.set-matrix-event` all already existed and only
# gained declarations, and the two at-rules it introduces (`@property
# --set-matrix-fade`, `@keyframes set-matrix-edge-fade`) are OPAQUE at-rules —
# cssom-parity skips them on BOTH sides (authoredHeads' GROUPING_AT branch and
# the symmetric CSSOM walk), so they contribute zero to this count by design.
# Recorded here rather than left silent: a ratchet whose number does not move
# on a real CSS change should say WHY in the same commit, or the next reader
# cannot tell a considered no-op from a forgotten bump.
# Re-measured 2026-07-31 (cch-w12-s3-sites-card-focus-perimeter): 1236 authored heads,
# MISSES 0. The +1 is ONE rule — `.inst-sites-card .site-row[data-id]:focus-visible` —
# giving a keyboard-focused row in the instance-detail Sites card a four-sided inset
# outline. Before it, that card's flush list treatment (`border: none` + `border-top`)
# zeroed the border the shared focus rule only re-COLOURS, so three of the four sides
# painted nothing. MISSES 0 confirms this is an unrecorded ADD, not a parity defect.
#
